filed history. Each employee generates $3.4M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $223K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Global Net Lease, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.5B market cap on $495M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +105.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $189M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 38 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 21.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 1243% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 71% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Global Net Lease (GNL) Could Be 32% Undervalued Following Third Quarter Earnings","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-gnl/global-net-lease/news/global-net-lease-gnl-could-be-32-undervalued-following-third","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794476274.943,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(GNL) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/GNL_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111126021802_1794424682.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794424682.0,"origin":"tiingo","senti